{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/324805-vs-supernatural-tv-series","id":324805,"title":"vs supernatural (tv series)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-28T15:03:08-08:00","id":324805,"title":"vs supernatural (tv series)","content":"Okay this show has some following. So let's say Sam and Dean run into a relatively benign pack of the forsaken or at least 1 member 3dot primal urge forsaken how would that go down, also said Forsaken has learned of a handful of those heart eater werewolves are in the area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1435-videopete","name":"videopete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T15:38:50-08:00","id":324833,"title":"","content":"Hardline answer: &quot;The Herd Must Not Know&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T20:25:39-08:00","id":325021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/324805-vs-supernatural-tv-series?p=324833#post324833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hardline answer: &quot;The Herd Must Not Know&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Except they've known for quite a while and have taken on shit arguably more powerful than Gauru. Hell, they've got a stock pile of guns with silver bullets in the back of their trunk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T21:09:56-08:00","id":325039,"title":"","content":"The Winchesters are definitely more on the, 'Kill first, don't bother asking questions,' side of things. So if that Forsaken doesn't get help, they're likely going to die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-29T07:56:44-08:00","id":325281,"title":"","content":"And then the forsaken will burn the town to the ground hunting them. Of Sam and dean attack the people the people will hit back. HARD. I'd imagine the pure might move on that as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-29T11:46:11-08:00","id":325455,"title":"","content":"The Winchesters have actually allowed a werewolf to live when they made sure she was not harming humans and could keep her curse under control. So there is a chance for a peaceful resolution, if the pack is willing to talk and explain and Sam can keep Dean under control after the first interraction. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If a battle was to go down I would expect that the brothers would have their hands full since Uratha are way more powerful than the show's werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-29T17:35:51-08:00","id":325671,"title":"","content":"In every case, my rule of thumb is to ask 'Who are the protagonists in this game?'<br /> <br /> If playing Sam and Dean - it's a hard fight but the werewolves eventually lose, teh Winchesters emerge bloodied but alive.<br /> <br /> If playing Hunter and Sam and Dean turn up - it's a hard fight but the werewolves eventually lose, after Sam and Dean are torn to shreds, or otherwise defeated and removed from consideration..<br /> <br /> If playing Werewolf and Sam and Dean turn up - it's a hard fight but the Winchesters are torn to shreds, or otherwise lose.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-29T20:32:32-08:00","id":325760,"title":"","content":"Interesting question. Unless there's some bigger threat in the area, I picture this doesn't end until either the pack or the Winchesters are corpses. Dean (and, to a lesser extent, Sam) aren't ones to get a &quot;monster's&quot; life story before deciding its kill-worthy. And the Uratha aren't usually considered to be very diplomatic when it comes to dealing with threats to their territory. If it comes to a confrontation (as opposed to the Uratha just leaving the boys alone to do whatever they're here to do then move on), then I don't see it ending peacefully, though I do see it ending piece-fully.<br /> <br /> If there is something else in the area. . . likely, misunderstanding, Let's You And Him Fight, get talking, sort things out, then they both go after the real Big Bad. In which case, the Real Big Bad gonna have a Real Big Bad Day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T11:27:38-08:00","id":326168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackheartz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/324805-vs-supernatural-tv-series?p=325455#post325455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Winchesters have actually allowed a werewolf to live when they made sure she was not harming humans and could keep her curse under control. So there is a chance for a peaceful resolution, if the pack is willing to talk and explain and Sam can keep Dean under control after the first interraction. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If a battle was to go down I would expect that the brothers would have their hands full since Uratha are way more powerful than the show's werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well they have no qualms about going head to head against Angels which pretty much rape everything else in the show. If they have access to The Colt, it's a one shot kill, too!<br /> <br /> On another note, here's their resume of &quot;Scion-tier&quot; stuff they've defeated.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Arch Angels<br /> <br /> Pagan Gods<br /> <br /> Leviathans<br /> <br /> A Knight of Hell<br /> <br /> War, Famine, and Pestilence<br /> <br /> They managed to bind Death, short lived as it was<br /> <br /> Anything else I'm missing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-30-2014, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T11:57:50-08:00","id":326190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/324805-vs-supernatural-tv-series?p=326168#post326168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well they have no qualms about going head to head against Angels which pretty much rape everything else in the show. If they have access to The Colt, it's a one shot kill, too!<br /> <br /> On another note, here's their resume of &quot;Scion-tier&quot; stuff they've defeated.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Arch Angels<br /> <br /> Pagan Gods<br /> <br /> Leviathans<br /> <br /> A Knight of Hell<br /> <br /> War, Famine, and Pestilence<br /> <br /> They managed to bind Death, short lived as it was<br /> <br /> Anything else I'm missing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but it is <i><b>their show</b></i> right? In many stories they were clocked in plot armor, against most of their foes they had tools(spells, weapons, substances) that delivered one-shots or binded them completely even though the creatures power levels were sky-high etc.<br /> <br /> Obviously the outcome, as Bunyip said, is more or less determined or predetermined by who the &quot;protagonists&quot; of the story are supposed to be and what the purpose of the story actually is. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T03:29:48-08:00","id":326803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackheartz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/324805-vs-supernatural-tv-series?p=326190#post326190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously the outcome, as Bunyip said, is more or less determined or predetermined by who the &quot;protagonists&quot; of the story are supposed to be and what the purpose of the story actually is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this. Obviously, protagonists can fail, the dice can go against them, and they can be killed. However, my default assumption is that they have the best chance of success.If they can't make it happen, probably no one can.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T10:22:38-08:00","id":328384,"title":"","content":"Even outside of the question of who the protagonist is, there's plenty of arguement for the fight between the Winchesters and a pack of werewolves being more even than you might expect from just looking at the Winchester's track record. Like Black Heartz said, they defeated several incredibly powerful entities by taking advantage of rituals and special objects of occult significance. World of Darkness models this extremely well with bans and banes, as well as some of the group tactics in the Hunter line. My point is, Sam and Dean should be regarded as EXTREMELY experience Hunters, with various occult resource merits, probably even some occult armory from the spirit section of GMC. They have defeated Pagan Gods, which in world of darkness roughly translates as &quot;Rank 4+ ephemeral entity&quot;. Which they defeated by being well prepared. Entities that werewolves with enough experience have the potential to stand against directly. So a conflict between Winchesters and Werewolves boils down to how they find out about one another, whether their interests clash, and how much prep time each group has to find out about the other. The Winchesters have a knack for using mundane resources to find monster's weaknesses, they might use those to find the werewolves totem ban and use it to their advantage, things like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T06:33:37-08:00","id":329163,"title":"","content":"I haven't watched Supernatural so am not aware of the Winchesters' particular level of capability, but if they are humans then they are likely to suffer issues in dealing with Lunacy. That said, even normal humans can be a very definite threat to werewolves, depending on how well-equipped and canny they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T14:20:54-08:00","id":329545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/324805-vs-supernatural-tv-series?p=329163#post329163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't watched Supernatural so am not aware of the Winchesters' particular level of capability, but if they are humans then they are likely to suffer issues in dealing with Lunacy. That said, even normal humans can be a very definite threat to werewolves, depending on how well-equipped and canny they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Winchesters have absurdly high Willpower - probably from all those shenanigans with saving one another from death. I think that Dean would have like WP 10 and Sam WP 9. They are ( after 10 seasons ) practically immune to Lunacy and similar effects, as they seen everything. They confronted almost everything similar to World of Darkness denizens and they now major problem is how to kill King of Hell or restore peace in Heaven.<br /> <br /> The other talk is when we look on them in season 1 &amp; 2 - then they can be spooked, they do not have all the knowledge and stuff they get from all the seasons. They are much more approachable. And more like typical Hunters in <b>Vigil</b>.<br /> <br /> To me, now ( season 10 ) Winchesters are almost unkillable, unless totally taken by surprise. It's even reason why screenwriters add new Hunters as supporting cast - in last episode we saw Jodi and Dona joining the case guys worked - because they logically need to become more mentor figures in Hunters community. And brothers seems more and more alien even to humans with they views on the world they live in.<br /> <br /> My bet is this - if Winchesters get time to think an research ( in the Bunker or Internet ) pack would be taken out by their tactics, calls to some other Hunters, and using pack Totem Ban and Banes. Silver machetes would also go in work.<br /> <br /> There is some chance for pack to surprise the brothers and then Gauru and Gifts ( not shown in series ) should move the favor to their side. But <b>only</b> if they get the guys of guard. Other way they will be killed. If not by the brothers ( or their, literal, guardian angel ), surely by all the Hunters they know and that look over for them, from time to time...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-03-2014, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T15:46:35-08:00","id":330576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/324805-vs-supernatural-tv-series?p=329163#post329163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't watched Supernatural so am not aware of the Winchesters' particular level of capability, but if they are humans then they are likely to suffer issues in dealing with Lunacy. That said, even normal humans can be a very definite threat to werewolves, depending on how well-equipped and canny they are.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If I'm not mistaken, the only foe they haven't killed outright was Lucifer, who straight up bust into a hotel filled with Pagan Gods, and painted the fucking walls with them. Instead, Sam and Dean had to open a portal to hell and shove him through it. They acquired the means to do this by Death giving Dean his ring, and teaching him how to combine it with the other 3 to cast the spell.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sam and Dean were raised since childhood to hunt monsters, with Dean in particular joining their father on hunts when he was just a boy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 12-04-2014, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T10:26:01-08:00","id":331265,"title":"","content":"Everything after season 5 was like the Matrix sequels for me. Enjoyable in a &quot;this is more of the thing I like!&quot; kind of way, but also painfully clear that the story really would have been better if it had just ended when it was originally planed to. Anyway, going off of seasons 1-5 Sam and Dean, and assuming this happens on an episode of Supernal rather than in a game of Werewolf...<br /> <br /> I'd say Sam would feel sympathetic towards them, Dean would try to convince him they're monsters and that means they need to be killed, Sam would point out that most Hunters would say the same about him, they'd get into a fight and split up for a while, Bobby would call them idjits and tell them how important family is, they'd get back together, and kill the whole pack. Though they might let one live if their backstory was tragic enough and they promised never to eat people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T11:54:25-08:00","id":331365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/324805-vs-supernatural-tv-series?p=331265#post331265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything after season 5 was like the Matrix sequels for me. Enjoyable in a &quot;this is more of the thing I like!&quot; kind of way, but also painfully clear that the story really would have been better if it had just ended when it was originally planed to. Anyway, going off of seasons 1-5 Sam and Dean, and assuming this happens on an episode of Supernal rather than in a game of Werewolf...<br /> <br /> I'd say Sam would feel sympathetic towards them, Dean would try to convince him they're monsters and that means they need to be killed, Sam would point out that most Hunters would say the same about him, they'd get into a fight and split up for a while, Bobby would call them idjits and tell them how important family is, they'd get back together, and kill the whole pack. Though they might let one live if their backstory was tragic enough and they promised never to eat people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Inversely, if this was a werewolf session, the Irraka would find out that the bros. have family trouble and a long-distance helper. Using this knowledge, they'd attempt to aggravate the arguments the two have, and coerce spirits into disabling or hampering their communications. Kind of like the...daeva? Whatever the monster was that pretended to be people's dead relatives over the phone.<br /> <br /> The fact that the brothers have silver weapons will be problematic, and should cause even the Rahu hesitation. Seems to me like the best thing to do is split the two up and take them out individually. Fortunately, the brothers have some sort of flaw that causes them to drop their weapons if you get the jump on them, so surprise actions are of phenomenal importance.<br /> <br /> Luring the brothers out into the woods would also be a good idea: getting them split up means that most of the pack can focus Gauru on each brother individually. Somebody probably needs to run interference on that angel that shows up in dire circumstances to help them though.<br /> <br /> Ultimately though it'll end in a brawl in a motel room or abandoned warehouse where somebody, probably one of the voices of reason and probably a girl that Sam fell in love with during the episode, is fatally wounded. This teaches both sides the importance of <i>something</i> and there are begrudging, angry goodbyes. Dean probably threatens to kill one of them if he ever sees them again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T15:40:10-08:00","id":331525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/324805-vs-supernatural-tv-series?p=331365#post331365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the...daeva? Whatever the monster was that pretended to be people's dead relatives over the phone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Crocotta. They're mythological dog-wolves that mimic human speech to lure people into the wild and eat them. It was one of the first times the show took a non-humanoid monster and completely anthropomorphized it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-05-2014, 11:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T19:26:59-08:00","id":331738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/324805-vs-supernatural-tv-series?p=331365#post331365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that the brothers have silver weapons will be problematic, and should cause even the Rahu hesitation. Seems to me like the best thing to do is split the two up and take them out individually. Fortunately, the brothers have some sort of flaw that causes them to drop their weapons if you get the jump on them, so surprise actions are of phenomenal importance.<br /> <br /> Luring the brothers out into the woods would also be a good idea: getting them split up means that most of the pack can focus Gauru on each brother individually. Somebody probably needs to run interference on that angel that shows up in dire circumstances to help them though.</div> </div> </div> </div>If this were a Forsaken game with PCs, they'd quickly discover that the brothers have relationship issues and like to have dramatic arguments in public, and in poorly-defended locations. The Forsaken would use their awesome new 2nd ed Gifts and hunter aspects to inflame tensions between the two brothers. Then, when they have their next public argument, the Rahu and Irraka would coordinate to put a bullet in each of the hunter's brains using high powered rifles from a couple-hundred yards away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T21:23:34-08:00","id":331892,"title":"","content":"And then they have drinks, because they have the rest of their evening open.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T20:14:49-08:00","id":408557,"title":"","content":"At this stage, I'm pretty sure the Winchesters and surprisingly humane &quot;Slashers&quot;. People don't auto kill them because one's a Charmer and they don't die from being thrown into a wall because they're Masks as well! Just without the Masks.....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My horror roleplaying blog with a strong focus on World of Darkness and Call of Cthulhu can be found here: <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\">http://stwildonrolep